From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:27:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gfxterm: a cursor that covers its cell

The cursor of gfxterm is a line of 2 pixels across the cell, at the
baseline of the font (draw_cursor()). On a large screen, or on a picture
of 1024x768 that a monitor of 2560x1440 scales up (which a firmware that
drives several displays at once may give it), it can hardly be seen: in
the editor of an entry and on the command line the place being edited
cannot be told.

The cursor is now a block over the whole cell, in the colour of the
text, with the character under it drawn in it in the colour of the
background made opaque (the black background of the terminal is
transparent in its text layer, gfxterm.c set_term_color(), so the
character would not show in the block otherwise). Where the cell holds
a wide character, the block is as wide as it. When the cursor leaves
the cell, the cell is painted again as it was, as before
(write_char()). The cursor is shown and hidden where it was; the menu
of gfxmenu hides it as before.
---
 grub-core/term/gfxterm.c | 35 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 27 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/grub-core/term/gfxterm.c b/grub-core/term/gfxterm.c
index 7fec1b0..5ed2f64 100644
--- a/grub-core/term/gfxterm.c
+++ b/grub-core/term/gfxterm.c
@@ -701,6 +701,9 @@ draw_cursor (int show)
   unsigned int height;
   unsigned int ascent;
   grub_video_color_t color;
+  struct grub_colored_char *p;
+  struct grub_font_glyph *glyph;
+  grub_uint8_t red, green, blue, alpha;
 
   write_char ();
 
@@ -711,23 +714,39 @@ draw_cursor (int show)
       >= virtual_screen.rows)
     return;
 
-  /* Ensure that cursor doesn't go outside of character box.  */
-  ascent = grub_font_get_ascent(virtual_screen.font);
-  if (ascent > virtual_screen.normal_char_height - 2)
-    ascent = virtual_screen.normal_char_height - 2;
+  /* Hades: the cursor is a block over the whole cell, the character under
+     it drawn in it in the colour of the background, made opaque (black,
+     the background of the editor and of the command line, is transparent
+     in the text layer).  A line of 2 pixels under the character, as it
+     was, can hardly be seen on a large screen or a picture that the
+     display scales up, and the place being edited cannot be told.  The
+     cell is painted again as it was when the cursor leaves it
+     (write_char ()).  */
+  ascent = grub_font_get_ascent (virtual_screen.font);
+  p = (virtual_screen.text_buffer
+       + virtual_screen.cursor_x
+       + virtual_screen.cursor_y * virtual_screen.columns);
+  glyph = p->code.base ? grub_font_construct_glyph (virtual_screen.font,
+						     &p->code) : NULL;
+  grub_errno = GRUB_ERR_NONE;
 
   /* Determine cursor properties and position on text layer. */
   x = virtual_screen.cursor_x * virtual_screen.normal_char_width;
-  width = virtual_screen.normal_char_width;
+  width = virtual_screen.normal_char_width
+    * (glyph ? calculate_character_width (glyph) : 1);
   color = virtual_screen.fg_color;
   y = ((virtual_screen.cursor_y + virtual_screen.total_scroll)
-       * virtual_screen.normal_char_height
-       + ascent);
-  height = 2;
+       * virtual_screen.normal_char_height);
+  height = virtual_screen.normal_char_height;
 
   /* Render cursor to text layer.  */
   grub_video_set_active_render_target (text_layer);
   grub_video_fill_rect (color, x, y, width, height);
+  if (glyph && grub_video_unmap_color (p->bg_color, &red, &green, &blue,
+				       &alpha) == GRUB_ERR_NONE)
+    grub_font_draw_glyph (glyph, grub_video_map_rgba (red, green, blue, 255),
+			  x, y + ascent);
+  grub_errno = GRUB_ERR_NONE;
   grub_video_set_active_render_target (render_target);
 
   /* Mark cursor to be redrawn.  */
